#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161689 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162123 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9040153-b66c-5c55-8854-8c5be0309720" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Expected Value Given a Conditional Mass Function"}] :question/id #uuid "07199b8b-32c6-59f5-b452-da48648cb799" :question/math-academy-id "e-10298" :question/problem "| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\, \\mid \\, 2)$ | $\\dfrac{2}{3}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ |\n\nFind the $\\textrm{E}\\big\\begin{bmatrix}Y \\, & \\, X=2\\big\\end{bmatrix}$ given that the conditional probability mass function $f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\, \\mid \\, 2)$ is shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "The conditional expected value of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}\\big\\begin{bmatrix}Y \\, & \\, X=x\\big\\end{bmatrix} = \\sum_{y} y \\, f_{Y \\mid X}(y \\, \\mid \\, x)\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE\\begin{bmatrix}Y & X = 2\\end{bmatrix} &= ∑_(y)yf_{Y\\mid X}(y \\mid 2) \\\\\n&= 1 \\cdot \\frac{2}{3} + 2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{3} \\\\\n&= \\frac{4}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161692 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162126 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "59bd2280-5028-5261-a9ed-61d01d80c29a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Expectation Using Row Totals"}] :question/id #uuid "2f074ddb-056a-51c6-b307-74df33f135f0" :question/math-academy-id "e-10305" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $X=1$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{2}{9}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{8}{27}$ | $\\dfrac{5}{27}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\dfrac{2}{27}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ |\n\nFind $\\textrm{E}\\big\\begin{bmatrix}Y \\, & \\, X=2\\big\\end{bmatrix}$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}\\big\\begin{bmatrix}Y \\, & \\, X=x\\big\\end{bmatrix} = \\sum_{y} y \\, f_{Y \\mid X}(y \\, \\mid \\, x)\n$$\n\nIn order to find $f_{Y \\mid X}(y \\, \\mid \\, x)$, let's first find the marginal distribution for $X$, corresponding to the row totals:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $f_X(x)$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $X=1$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{2}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{8}{27}$ | $\\dfrac{5}{27}$ | $\\dfrac{13}{27}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\dfrac{2}{27}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{5}{27}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x$ is\n\n$$\nf_{Y \\mid X}(y \\, \\mid \\, x) = \\dfrac{f(x,y)}{f_X(x)}\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding row total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x{:}$\n\n| $f_{Y \\mid X}(y \\, \\mid \\, x)$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |  |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $X=1$ | $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ | $\\dfrac{2}{3}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{8}{13}$ | $\\dfrac{5}{13}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\dfrac{2}{5}$ | $\\dfrac{3}{5}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE\\begin{bmatrix}Y & X = 2\\end{bmatrix} &= ∑_(y)yf_{Y\\mid X}(y \\mid 2) \\\\\n&= 1 \\cdot \\frac{8}{13} + 2 \\cdot \\frac{5}{13} \\\\\n&= \\frac{18}{13}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161699 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162133 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8e47d5ac-cb51-5259-ba41-6c407a992271" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Expectation Using Column Totals"}] :question/id #uuid "4de21bb7-7f18-56c4-9925-47459df6f049" :question/math-academy-id "e-10350" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{2}{9}$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ |\n\nFind $\\textrm{E}\\big\\begin{bmatrix}X \\, & \\, Y=1\\big\\end{bmatrix}$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional expected value of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}\\big\\begin{bmatrix}X \\, & \\, Y=y\\big\\end{bmatrix} = \\sum_{x} x \\, f_{X \\mid Y}(x \\, \\mid \\, y)\n$$\n\nIn order to find $f_{X \\mid Y}(x \\, \\mid \\, y)$, let's first find the marginal distribution for $Y$, corresponding to the column totals:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{2}{9}$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ |\n| $f_Y(y)$ | $\\dfrac{5}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{4}{9}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y$ is\n\n$$\nf_{X \\mid Y}(x \\, \\mid \\, y) = \\dfrac{f(x,y)}{f_Y(y)}\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding column total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y{:}$\n\n| $f_{X \\mid Y}(x \\, \\mid \\, y)$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{1}{5}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\dfrac{3}{5}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\dfrac{1}{5}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ |\n|  | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE\\begin{bmatrix}X & Y = 1\\end{bmatrix} &= ∑_(x)xf_{X\\mid Y}(x \\mid 1) \\\\\n&= 2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{5} + 4 \\cdot \\frac{3}{5} + 6 \\cdot \\frac{1}{5} \\\\\n&= \\frac{20}{5} \\\\\n&= 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162428 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162126 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "59bd2280-5028-5261-a9ed-61d01d80c29a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Expectation Using Row Totals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9887025-89a2-5bd7-a74f-b101df7d541c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159771} {:answer/id #uuid "e389798f-f44e-5b5b-afcd-2e7852474619" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159772} {:answer/id #uuid "04531933-c48e-5b18-b0b0-c0907b8ac81a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159773} {:answer/id #uuid "46a6904a-9a4b-5f70-b8cc-c0f4f9a23923" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159774} {:answer/id #uuid "6245a964-4af7-5b27-bc90-58eca4710df2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159775}] :answer-field/id #uuid "e55a32c3-ff9a-5ff5-80ee-6d10e0e5e4ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159770}] :question/id #uuid "449949db-2f44-58fe-9afc-0f4fff6f21fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-146248" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y = 0$ | $Y = 2$ | $Y = 4$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $X = 0$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{3}{18}$ | $\\frac{1}{18}$ |\n| $X = 2$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ |\n\nFind $E\\begin{bmatrix}Y & X = 2\\end{bmatrix}$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x, y)$ shown in the table above."}]}
